{{also|tipoff|tip-off}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|tips off|tipping off|tipped off}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[alert]] or [[inform]] someone, especially [[confidentially]].
#: ''An anonymous caller '''tipped off''' the police that the suspect would be in the area.''
# {{lb|en|basketball}} To put the ball in play by throwing it up between two opponents.
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[pour out]] (liquor).
#{{lb|en|transitive|and|intransitive|[[artisanal]] [[terminology]]}} In [[painting]], a brush technique for producing a flawless surface on a a wet coat of paint; a synonym for [[lay off]]

